{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them","id":1463143,"title":"How many pigs to feed a vampire without killing any of them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-08T13:33:17-07:00","id":1463143,"title":"How many pigs to feed a vampire without killing any of them?","content":"An high humanity vampire keeps a pig farm and regularly takes a bit of blood from several of them in order to keep himself feed without killing the animals.<br /> More or less how many pigs it would take to do that, taking in account the time needed to recover fully from a light blood loss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T14:00:39-07:00","id":1463150,"title":"","content":"I'd say most pigs have 2bp in them so maybe 8","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T15:15:56-07:00","id":1463162,"title":"","content":"I hope you were told there would be math. Because that's what I am doing.<br /> <br /> We know adult humans have around 10 pints of blood and a blood pool of 10. We also know that animal blood is less nutritious for vampires. Both Revised and V20 corebook say a domestic pig's blood pool is 3. Pigs are supposed to have around 7 pints of blood. To make the math easier we could say that every 2 pints of pig blood produces 1 point of blood pool. (Note the game is inconsistent on things. Draft horses have around 14 gallons of blood (about 112 pints) yet only provide 4 blood points. That's almost 30 pints of horse blood per blood point! If you want to explain that, maybe because the horse is a herbivore, it's blood is worth even less than that of a pig who is an omnivore that eats meat So not all animal blood is worth the same.)<br /> <br /> In real life, donating a pint of blood takes several months to recover. But the game says mortals will regain one blood point per day. Big difference. But it's the game's rule so we'll go with that. Now for pigs, I'd say because you have to drain more blood to get 1 blood point, it should take at least 2 days maybe 3 to recover.<br /> <br /> However, we're also told that vampires can't take more than 20% of a vessel's blood without harming the vessel. 20% of a pig's 3 blood pool is only 0.6 blood pool. So to get one blood point out of a pig, you risk killing that pig. But I'd rule that feeding equally on two pigs per night get's you that one point you need, and both pigs are just before the point where they'd be harmed.<br /> <br /> Now per the rules, if you feed on humans you only need 2 humans to avoid draining that person of blood. On one night you drain 1 point of blood from one human. The next night you drain another point of blood on the second human, and the first human's blood pool replenishes. The third night you can go back to the first human who has a replenished blood pool. So technically you just need two. I think that's cutting it too close as too many things can go wrong, so you'd likely really need 4 so you have some slack in case one of them gets sick or you need more than one point of blood for the night. (And this assumes the person doesn't resist with you taking what you need).<br /> <br /> For pigs, we know you need to feed on two per night. And the pigs would need at least 2 days to recover. So you need four more pigs to cover two more days before the first batch could be ready. That's six pigs. But just like with the humans, I think that's cutting it too close. You should have double the amount for emergencies and take into consideration something happening to the pigs.<br /> <br /> So I would say a vampire needs a minimum of 12 adult pigs to safely recover from low blood loss (1 per night). If you plan on burning more blood, you need more pigs.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's my logic anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T15:49:10-07:00","id":1463169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463162#post1463162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In real life, donating a pint of blood takes several months to recover. But the game says mortals will regain one blood point per day. Big difference. But it's the game's rule so we'll go with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who donates to the Red Cross regularly, I can explain this one.<br /> <br /> Lost blood volume will indeed recover in about 24 hours, for the first time or two. The mineral reserves in our marrow that are used to build those blood cells, however, take longer to recover and ongoing depletion will result in anemia and similar symptoms.<br /> <br /> In game terms this means a human can physically recover from the effects of being fed on once in a day or two, but would suffer illness if they were drained repeatedly without their body having a chance to restock the minerals and proteins needed to keep constructing new blood cells and that\u2019s the part that can take a month or two.<br /> <br /> The Red Cross doing 8 weeks between donations is more a \u201cbetter safe than sorry\u201d standard. Most people will recover the lost minerals in 4-5 weeks, but could be quicker or longer depending on diet. 8 weeks is essentially the outside timeframe where even someone on a mediocre diet (but still healthy enough to donate) will have fully recovered with time to spare.<br /> <br /> As such, a dedicated herd member on a high iron and protein diet could be safely fed from at a rate of about a point per month with little risk (barring underlying health issues).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T16:02:28-07:00","id":1463170,"title":"","content":"Black Fox's math is solid.<br /> <br /> Though if you want to add a bit on the realism front: give your pigs a lot of supplemental iron (though not too much because iron poisoning is also a thing).<br /> <br /> The biggest bottlenecks in mammalian blood regeneration are water intake and iron intake. Water is something your pigs should have constant access too anyway. Mammals are capable of regenerating all of the core blood components in a day or two... but don't store significant amounts of iron to fuel a ramp up in red blood cell production. The iron stores are also what takes the longest time to replenish in the blood regeneration process (we go through a lot of iron daily and siphon very little of it for storage). The biggest risk of repeated low level blood loss is iron-deficiency induced anemia.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter to the magical process of taking vitae, but since that requires draining blood and all, if you're going to try to feed on a minimal herd, it's worth keeping in mind if you want to keep an eye on such details.<br /> <br /> Or... what Chris just said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-08-2021, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T16:19:06-07:00","id":1463173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463162#post1463162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you were told there would be math. Because that's what I am doing.<br /> <br /> We know adult humans have around 10 pints of blood and a blood pool of 10. We also know that animal blood is less nutritious for vampires. Both Revised and V20 corebook say a domestic pig's blood pool is 3. Pigs are supposed to have around 7 pints of blood. To make the math easier we could say that every 2 pints of pig blood produces 1 point of blood pool. (Note the game is inconsistent on things. Draft horses have around 14 gallons of blood (about 112 pints) yet only provide 4 blood points. That's almost 30 pints of horse blood per blood point! If you want to explain that, maybe because the horse is a herbivore, it's blood is worth even less than that of a pig who is an omnivore that eats meat So not all animal blood is worth the same.).</div> </div> </div> </div>My own interpretation/head canon is that the Beast specifically craves human blood and so nothing else is as effective. Animal blood is just a stop-gap, and one likely to fail at the worst possible time. Just for thematic reasons, I've never really even liked the idea of stored/bagged blood being as effective/potent as freshly taken, but that is just personal preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T16:51:24-07:00","id":1463176,"title":"","content":"The books explicitly say stored blood is less nourishing that fresh so... that's not just personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T18:47:26-07:00","id":1463181,"title":"","content":"Amassing all that and assuming the best interpretation of the rules (since our goal here is for this to work, but within the rules).<br /> <br /> Minimum Safe Herd = 2 pigs for 1 BP/month. So you need 60 pigs for basic necessities, plus 2 pigs for your expectations in excess Blood intake.<br /> <br /> For ideal safety, 120 pigs would let you give each pig 2 months to recover, so their health is better cared for. Consider that not only you may need more blood, but also that you herd may have problems of their own, so at the very least twice that would be better, a whopping 240 pigs. Ideally I would keep my herd at 600 or more whenever possible.<br /> <br /> Now, a typical US pig farm actually houses about 8k pigs. They're factory farms, but that nonetheless means that having and handling that many pigs isn't completely unreasonable. You may have to deal with it being a production farm, not just your yard or something, as that many pigs will have several costs and aren't really cheap or subtle to keep, but they are a viable option.<br /> <br /> You only have to keep one last thing in mind while feeding on pigs: <b>they are omnivores capable and whiling on eating humans, both freshly killed or corpses, so it isn't impossible for a careless vampire to end up on their menu</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T19:04:23-07:00","id":1463182,"title":"","content":"Honestly, with the math the way it is, every factory farm should be controlled by vampires with employees who routinely draw blood of the animals for vampiric consumption. This place would be helpful to the vampire controller, their allies, and any who wished to buy or trade favors for blood. Even those who hate drinking animal blood may need to occasionally take a trip to the blood factory, and with 8,000 pigs available, there will always be blood on tap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T21:03:21-07:00","id":1463193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463176#post1463176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books explicitly say stored blood is less nourishing that fresh so... that's not just personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some recollection of that from revised, but don't have any books handy to check. I can't recall if 1st or 2nd ed made a distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T23:45:14-07:00","id":1463197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463182#post1463182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, with the math the way it is, every factory farm should be controlled by vampires with employees who routinely draw blood of the animals for vampiric consumption. This place would be helpful to the vampire controller, their allies, and any who wished to buy or trade favors for blood. Even those who hate drinking animal blood may need to occasionally take a trip to the blood factory, and with 8,000 pigs available, there will always be blood on tap.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC you can't use animal blood in cold storage, it must either be human or fresh blood. And with 1 BP being enough to kill a pig from blood loss, letting other vampire drink from your delicate animals isn't a smart option. But selling the pigs totally is, and kind of the point with a pig farm if you really go all the way to have one. You can then have a &quot;dinner room&quot; for undead buyers.<br /> <br /> Overall the idea of vampires feeding on stock before they're cut isn't BS. Most meat nowadays come from factories where the animals need to be drained anyway for sanitary reasons. Cursed bites aren't exactly safe, but also nothing that health officials can detect. It is an interesting plot hook to have such farms and explore what would be the effects of the Curse of Caine tainting human food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T00:04:08-07:00","id":1463200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463193#post1463193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some recollection of that from revised, but don't have any books handy to check. I can't recall if 1st or 2nd ed made a distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can confirm that 2nd edition core already states that, with the caveat that blood from Ancients may keep their quality far longer. I can't say the page for sure because my copy is in Portuguese, but it must be around 180, just before the Systems chapter.<br /> <br /> And indeed it is the very same text at least since then, it is the same (untranslated) in V20, and it never got down to actual rules on how exactly the cold storage affect the blood in terms of BP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T00:36:03-07:00","id":1463205,"title":"","content":"There's nothing that actually says you can't store animal blood for use, but with the idea that stored blood is even less nourishing, the sheer volume of it you'd have to consume starts to get a bit ridiculous.<br /> <br /> While I know pulling from VtR isn't always the best or what people are looking for, the VtR 2e rule for stored blood has a nice thematic twist to it: To get 1 vitae out of cold blood, you need to consume your Blood Potency x 2 the equivalent amount of warm blood. This isn't hard to translate to pre-V5 by just using your dots in the Generation background instead (though I'd put that at a min. of 1 unless you take the Thin Blood or 14th/15th Gen Flaws).<br /> <br /> It actually puts a bit of counter pressure on dumping all your Background dots in Generation (starting at Generation 8 would mean you need to consume an entire adult human's worth of cold blood for 1 bp, so stored blood goes out the window as an effective strategy), and adds a bit of a practical and grounded psychological side to the worries about the every diluting blood in higher Generations. Older and lower Generation vampires simply can't practically sup on stored pigs blood purchased from a butcher, and have to feed on warm blood, increasing their alienation from humanity, and making Humanity more difficult for them, while a 14th Gen or a Thin-blood can basically get buy on a couple pints of cold pigs blood a night. It might not be pleasing to the palate, but it allows them to act more human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T01:13:30-07:00","id":1463208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463205#post1463205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing that actually says you can't store animal blood for use, but with the idea that stored blood is even less nourishing, the sheer volume of it you'd have to consume starts to get a bit ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed my error when I was consulting the book for the previous post, but run the math and it gets ridiculous. Drinking from a cow is 7 pints per BP, about 3.5 litters, this is enough to cause water intoxication in a human if taken at once. If we assume cold storage blood as 30% less potent (you need about half again in volume for the same benefit), it's 5 litters, the entire blood of an adult. I have a water bottle that size here and I'm literally looking at the sheer amount of blood it is. For 1 BP.<br /> <br /> As for the bottle, I'm lazy to get water all the time so that is my personal water bottle that I recharge with mineral water. Maybe I'll start to dye it red after those numbers.<br /> <br /> The worse part is that by RAW your consumption speed is only limited by effective BP and not by volume. That means that the weaker the blood, the faster you drink, the stronger the slower. If you feed from bottled low Gen blood you have to sip slowly as if you were taking medicine, but you can suck 10,5 litters (21 pints) from a cow in 3 seconds!<br /> <br /> One last thing: to this date the game still says that cold storage blood is less nutritious, but also that 1 bag of plasma is 1 BP. Well, 1 bag of plasma is about half a pint, so it is actually stronger than warm blood... why I'm not surprised?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T09:11:17-07:00","id":1463231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463197#post1463197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC you can't use animal blood in cold storage, it must either be human or fresh blood. And with 1 BP being enough to kill a pig from blood loss, letting other vampire drink from your delicate animals isn't a smart option. But selling the pigs totally is, and kind of the point with a pig farm if you really go all the way to have one. You can then have a &quot;dinner room&quot; for undead buyers.<br /> <br /> Overall the idea of vampires feeding on stock before they're cut isn't BS. Most meat nowadays come from factories where the animals need to be drained anyway for sanitary reasons. Cursed bites aren't exactly safe, but also nothing that health officials can detect. It is an interesting plot hook to have such farms and explore what would be the effects of the Curse of Caine tainting human food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are a few ways that could be handled. The vampire who owns the factory farm could have some ghouls on staff who are essentially pig phlebotomists, who can draw blood from several pigs on demand and give it to the vampires while it\u2019s still warm and fresh. Alternatively, the pigs are there to get slaughtered anyway and I assume that a factory farm with thousands of pigs is constantly slaughtering (or sending to get slaughtered) pigs and breeding new ones. If a vampire comes and needs blood, then they just slaughter a few pigs and let the vampire drink. I don\u2019t know if this kind of factory farm slaughters the pigs on location or ships them off to a separate location to be slaughtered and processed, but where ever that slaughtering happens is where the vampire can drink. If a pig is going to be slaughtered anyway, and drained of its blood, then I suppose the vampire could just drink it dry first. It probably wouldn\u2019t result in any health concerns for the meat, though I suppose if that were a risk then the farmer owner could just charge extra for the service, the extra charge could include the value of the wasted meat. So the dinner room idea makes sense. <br /> <br /> If vampires can drink refrigerated pig blood, it makes the process more convenient, but it\u2019s not really necessary.<br /> <br /> The science in this situation gets a bit strange, it\u2019s almost like vampires need to be able to urinate to drink animal blood. A horse has 4 blood points, so a vampire could drink two horses dry and still have room for more. Where does all of the liquid go? Real life mosquitoes can actually excrete the water in the blood they drink to concentrate it, but that doesn\u2019t seem like what vampires would do. I think a simple way to handle cold blood might be to have it count as half as potent, meaning that it would take more than one blood bag to make a blood point.<br /> <br /> I was looking at animals in the V20 book and it looks like bobcats have blood pools of 4. This means bobcats have blood which is more potent per volume than humans. I think a bobcat farm would still be inconvenient compared to pigs though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T11:28:25-07:00","id":1463243,"title":"","content":"Well, I wasn't thinking about an industrial pig farm, which is quite costly.<br /> I guess that more or less 120 pigs with some iron supplements could do the trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T12:52:05-07:00","id":1463249,"title":"","content":"Feasible, indeed. It would be a safe choice. You'll still have costs, though, as those pigs need care, including veterinarian care, and Ghouling them still carries the actual risk of them devouring you, this is no joke. Although the precise numbers aren't known, every year there are cases all around the world of pigs killing and eating humans on purpose, and they coordinate to do so. So safety will also have a cost.<br /> <br /> The advantage of an industrial pig farm is to have a return for your investment, as a smaller number of pigs will just drain financial resources and require specialized care and helpers anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T15:38:49-07:00","id":1463257,"title":"","content":"Yeah, 100 pigs is going to require multiple employees as well as quality facilities and equipment, feed, waste disposal, medical care, etc. If you just use it for your own blood supply, the entire operation is more suspicious. If it\u2019s an actual profitable pig farm, then it can support itself with mundane business and then provide a source for favors in the vampiric world too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T17:30:06-07:00","id":1463268,"title":"","content":"If the venture is based on pragmatism rather than ethics having a pig farm could certainly come in handy for offering body disposal services to vampires that aren't opposed to feeding on live humans.<br /> <br /> I think most animals' aversion to the undead would counter any danger pigs might present to the vampire(s), though panic might make it a lot more difficult to feed on them directly. Clearly having Animalism would make the whole operation run more smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 10-09-2021, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T18:35:02-07:00","id":1463273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463268#post1463268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most animals' aversion to the undead would counter any danger pigs might present to the vampire(s), though panic might make it a lot more difficult to feed on them directly. Clearly having Animalism would make the whole operation run more smoothly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt pigs wold really be shy from feeding on vampires, but they really can and do feed on corpses. Panicked pigs also aren't a pretty thing as you can end up being stomped to death. Animalism is a very good choice to make this operation run smoothly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27051_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27051\" data-vbnamecard=\"27051\">Solomon Draak</a>, this operation is absolutely feasible, but the thing is that it is too big to run on anonymity even with 60 pigs, and the costs are high. You don't need to go full industrial if you don't want to, but the best way to conceal here is to have a farm that works for real and make some profit with your pigs. Which is also easy enough to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T18:35:30-07:00","id":1463274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463243#post1463243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that more or less 120 pigs with some iron supplements could do the trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we're at a rather large number of pigs than my original guess of 6-12 (and thanks for everyone's contribution here), there's another factor to think of that may reduce that number to a more manageable size.<br /> <br /> Instead of just keeping such a large number of pigs static, you can breed new pigs and replace the old ones. So as long as the vampire is willing to kill a large number of pigs, he doesn't need to keep them all alive. He can replace them as he uses them up.<br /> <br /> I know nothing about pig farming except what I just read online so take everything with a healthy grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Female pigs go into estrus about once a month. It takes about 120 days to gestate. Average pig litter size at small farms is around 8-10 per litter, and it seems the total number of pigs born per mother per year is around 33 and weaned is around 26. To be safe, let's say each sow gives birth to 24 pigs a year. Each pig needs to grow about six months to get to their mature full weight. So there is a really fast turnaround.<br /> <br /> Assume we keep 2 male boar for breeding (1 needed and the other as back up) and the rest will be sows. You could stagger them out so each month a different sow becomes pregnant. It then takes that sow 120 days to give birth and another 180 days for that litter to become mature. If you simply have 6 sows (each giving birth twice a year), you can probably produce almost 100 pigs a year. That will produce a new batch of 8 every month. That's a lot of extra pigs.<br /> <br /> So you don't need to keep all the pigs alive. You probably want a breeding population of only 8 pigs or so that you never feed on. Young pigs won't produce enough blood points so you'll need to wait until they're mature. But assuming you're not in start up mode, that's providing you with 8 full pigs a month. Each has 3 blood points. That is 24 blood points. Almost enough for a full month. You're short by about 77 blood points a year which is about 29 more pigs. To boost that up and provide some redundancy, let's say you need 40 more pigs a year. 3 more sows will provide more than that over a year.<br /> <br /> So we'll need a breeding pair of boars and 9 sows. That's 11 pigs. Plus six months supply worth of pigs before they get used up. That's another 48 pigs or so. To make things simple, let's put the total at 60 pigs in any given month, most of whom will be killed over the year and turned into bacon you can sell after you drain their blood. You are also reproducing enough that you can easily replace your breeding pigs whenever needed. And you have some slack. Most of those 60 pigs are juvenile so there'll be less feed to provide and waste to remove.<br /> <br /> So as long as the vampire doesn't cry while reading Charlotte's Web, he can make do with a lower number than the 120. It'll just take more active management. But the lower number of pigs makes it easier to manage. He could pay some daytime farm laborers to do the work during the day while the vampire sleeps and put out pay envelopes.<br /> <br /> Instead of feeding once a night to draw one blood point, he'll feed once every three nights and drain an entire adult pig dry. He can then butcher it and presumably sell it.<br /> <br /> And assuming he is living in a rural area with other farms nearby, he could lower the number of pigs even more if he is content with migrating between his neighbor's farms and taking less harmful amounts of blood from other livestock, rotating a long time between different animals. Or have some cows on the farm as well that he feeds on occasionally. It'll be a terrible diet for a vampire, but he can avoid feeding on humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T19:39:35-07:00","id":1463277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463274#post1463274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'll be a terrible diet for a vampire, but he can avoid feeding on humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>This vampire will avoid feeding on humans, create jobs, give the pigs a fairly humane death (the Kiss instead of a shot in the head if the pig is lucky), doing all the managing in the farm, which is generally a better treatment, and reduce the hazardous waste produced (pig blood is highly infectious) and will literally be paid to feed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T22:42:01-07:00","id":1463283,"title":"","content":"Just consume the pigs...<br /> <br /> Truth be told you'll need around 15 pigs just to get 9 blood points, in case of emergencies. This is assuming the ST of your table allows to take fractional blood points. If not the the pigs will suffer side effects every time. I actually recommend cows for blood because of the clean math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T11:44:25-07:00","id":1463334,"title":"","content":"Mabye there are easier animals to do the trick with? Like, sheeps, goats, rabbits?<br /> I heard that cows are relatively frail, they must be protected from weather and illness.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T12:41:28-07:00","id":1463341,"title":"","content":"Cows aren't particularly fragile. Large scale cattle production just tends to care more about end products than matching breed to the location, or giving cows the space they need to avoid diseases spreading through the herd. Any animal is highly subject to illness if cramped too closely together. Get the right breed for your climate, and have appropriate sized pastures for the size of your herd, and cows are plenty healthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T20:12:22-07:00","id":1463369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463143-how-many-pigs-to-feed-a-vampire-without-killing-any-of-them?p=1463334#post1463334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mabye there are easier animals to do the trick with? Like, sheeps, goats, rabbits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely, that was actually far easier than I thought it would be once we got to the math and to look at farms.<br /> <br /> Whatever you choose you won't escape the basic facts, Kindred aren't meant to subsist on animals easily. You'll always run on the base necessity of relatively large numbers, and large numbers of animals will always need a heft maintenance because they're large numbers.<br /> <br /> You want to have a single dog? With some luck a healthy stray may live more than 15 years without a veterinarian. But 50 dogs? You'll need a veterinarian at hand at least every week. It will be cheaper per dog, but will also be unavoidable. The kind of facilities, costs, maintenance, everything changes when you scale up numbers.<br /> <br /> And to live on animal blood you'll have to scale up. You'll still need, to begin with, to give any mammal 1 to 2 months to recover from the loss of iron. Smaller animals recover fast, but also suffer more with any wound or loss, even if proportions are kept, so it remains as a good rule of thumb. That means you'll need 30 to 60 no matter what just so you can feed every day. No animal will give you more than 5 BP, so 30 to 60 is an unavoidable floor for your plan.<br /> <br /> If you plan on killing the animals and replenish the stock things always get easier, but then you still need numbers and management all the same. And vets, helpers, costs...<br /> <br /> This is totally doable, and maybe I'll put this to use in my Changeling chronicle when I start to work with the Prodigals. But it's only easy depending on your definition of easy. Plenty of people in rural areas live by such farms, so it won't be low-profile, but won't be high-profile, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}